es using Data(contentsOf:) and NSURLConnection were accepted.\\n   - The existing negative test at scripts/tests/test_relay_supply_chain.py:78-89 covers only URLSession plus a literal HTTPS URL and does not cover disabled scan scope or other common download paths.\\n   - Consequence: the audit can claim zero application-runtime code download while scanning no files or while missing ordinary Foundation fetch APIs.\\n\\n4. Mutable dependency URLs other than latest are accepted (developer contract, immutable-source requirement).\\n   - scripts/relay_supply_chain.py:128-133 rejects only a small token list.\\n   - Replacing the pinned build-recipe URL with https://github.com/relux-works/relux-tunnel/tree/main was accepted.\\n   - Consequence: a regenerated provenance record may contain a mutable branch URL while the validator reports it as immutable.\\n\\n## Required remediation\\n\\n- Bind every fixed component ID to the exact authoritative revision/hash/source/license/text-hash/notice/distribution record. Add negative tests for each cross-record mismatch, including relay source, build recipe, compiler, and standard library.\\n- Enforce the approved SPDX/license-text/notice mapping per component rather than accepting arbitrary non-empty license identifiers. Add mismatched-ID/text and unapproved-ID tests.\\n- Make runtime audit coverage immutable and non-empty. Cover all application/runtime source roots and relevant source kinds, and add negative tests for disabled roots/extensions plus representative Foundation and process-based executable-fetch surfaces. Avoid claiming semantic zero-download coverage from the current three-pattern scan.\\n- Validate source URLs structurally against their pinned revision/version or a strict per-component allowlist. Add branch, tag, latest, query, fragment, and placeholder negative cases.\\n- Regenerate all outputs and re-run the full focused gates and deterministic double-generation check.\\n\\n## Independent positive evidence\\n\\n- Pinned source commit 58676a23e2e0fb3fcc1b5005d59c6ed56d3c0096 and recipe commit 4326036a26a515d5d349e669574323d4d1c7259c are available ancestors with matching Git trees and file hashes.\\n- Go 1.26.5 go list independently resolves exactly the eight declared compiled Go files; relay/go.mod is standard-library-only and supplies the ninth declared repository input.\\n- Current inventory, provenance, notice, asset-source, and Swift output hashes are byte-identical across two generation runs.\\n- Current product notices cover the relay MIT license and statically linked Go standard-library BSD-3-Clause text.\\n- The M2/M5 boundary names the required concrete downstream signing, notarization, release-attestation, and distribution-approval tasks.\\n\\n## Commands and exit codes\\n\\n- make relay-supply-chain-audit relay-supply-chain-test relay-asset-manifest-test — exit 0; 8 Python supply-chain tests, 26 Python asset-manifest tests, and 4 Swift manifest tests passed.\\n- make relay-shell-test relay-shell-vet — exit 0; all relay packages, 35 release-tool tests, and Go vet passed.\\n- swift build — exit 0.\\n- Python compilation, Black check, Swift format lint, Actionlint, JSON parsing, and git diff --check — exit 0.\\n- Two consecutive make relay-supply-chain-generate runs — exit 0; all five output hash sets identical.\\n- Adversarial in-memory validator probe — exit 0; seven invalid cases above were reported ACCEPTED.\\n- task-board validate — exit 0 while reporting one PARENT_STATUS_MISMATCH for EPIC-260715-2lz67t. The epic is blocked by EPIC-260715-2mqgvm and EPIC-260715-3810we, so this is the pre-existing aggregate/dependency constraint described by the producer, not a reason to weaken validation and not the basis of this rejection.\\n\\n## Safety\\n\\nNo signing, notarization, attestation, publishing, app/provider installation or launch, VPN mutation, network routing change, credential access, or network fetch was performed.\\n\", description=\"Independent reviewer verdict and handoff evidence\")'" in /Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel
